  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/amal.elgammal/ontologies/2025/3/untitled-ontology-31#ProductSpecification">
    <rdfs:comment>This class holds the technical or regulatory specifications for a product — such as dimensions, material, compliance standards, etc. One product may have one or multiple specs depending on how you model it.

ProductSpecification can be a versioned class — so modeling a version history via isReplacedBy is useful for traceability.

hasDocumentLink can store a path to a file in a DMS or ERP.</rdfs:comment>
    <j.0:blueprintClass>ProductBlueprint</j.0:blueprintClass>
  </owl:Class>
